{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And they shall spread the garment.</b> This is not an actual garment, but rather they debate this matter until the things are worn through like a garment. So Rashi explained." "<b>But</b> the Ramban explained that it is an actual garment, for otherwise what business does the mother have to come to the court? It would suffice for the father to press his claim and say, 'My daughter I gave to this man,' and the mother is not a party to his suit. Rather, because it is an actual garment, and it is the way of women to deal in this matter and to be expert in bloodstains, therefore the mother is mentioned in the passage. And this is the language of the verse, which first mentions, ״ולקח אבי הנערה ואמה והוציאו״ — 'and the girl's father and mother shall take and bring out' — it speaks of both of them; and afterward it returns to the father alone, ״ואמר אבי הנערה״ — 'and the girl's father shall say'; and it returns and says, ״ופרשו השמלה״ — 'and they shall spread the garment' — in both of them, for after the father has set forth his claims in court, he takes hold of the garment that his wife brought under her clothing, and they both spread it out before the court. End quote."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:23.610636129Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}